hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2775","Narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm, narrated to us Yaḥyā (meaning Ibn Saʿīd), narrated to us Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, narrated to us ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā (RA), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) performed ʿUmrah, circumambulated the House (the Kaʿbah), then went out and performed the ṣaʿy (walking between Ṣafā and Marwah). We (the Companions) shielded him from the people of Makkah lest any of them throw something at him or harm him. I heard him supplicating against the confederates (the Quraysh and their allies), saying:\n\n*\O Allāh"," You Who sent down the Book and Who is swift in reckoning"," defeat the confederates! O Allāh"," defeat them and cause their feet to slip!\""*\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
